language 0.1.0
module data
  means
    Logical organisation of data: kinds of values, the structure of records,
    their identity and the rules of admissibility, independent of how the data
    is stored, transferred or displayed.

entity schema : thing
  means
    schema: a formal description of the structure and constraints of a body of
    data.

entity record : thing
  means
    record: a composite value made of named fields and representing one
    logical data object.

entity field : thing
  means
    field: a named part of a record, having a definite type and value.

entity identifier : thing
  means
    identifier: a value or a set of values distinguishing one record from
    others within an established scope.

entity constraint : thing
  means
    constraint: a rule determining which data values or combinations of values
    are admissible.

entity classification : thing
  means
    classification: a named category determining how data is handled according
    to its meaning or sensitivity.
